<section class="cms-section cms-quality-section" id="quality"><div class="container cms-quality-layout"><div class="cms-quality-collage"><img class="cms-quality-main" src="/images/manufacturing-split/real-assets/machined-structure.jpg" alt="Structural component set up for machining in the company profile" width="869" height="580" loading="lazy" /><img class="cms-quality-inset" src="/images/manufacturing-split/real-assets/laser-cutting.jpg" alt="Plate cutting equipment from REALJET’s company profile" width="1050" height="580" loading="lazy" /><span>Drawing → Process → Acceptance</span></div><div class="cms-quality-copy"><span class="cms-eyebrow">Quality starts with the drawing</span><h2>Define the fit.<br /> Then plan the checks.</h2><p>The inspection plan follows your part’s critical features and delivery condition. Confirm what needs to be measured, when it needs to be checked and which records are required.</p><dl><div><dt>Material &amp; revision</dt><dd>Confirm the drawing revision, material specification and required certificates.</dd></div><div><dt>Geometry &amp; mating</dt><dd>Agree datums, critical faces, locating bores, hole patterns and any trial fit.</dd></div><div><dt>Finish &amp; release</dt><dd>Review weld appearance, finish, masking, identification and packing against the order.</dd></div></dl><a class="cms-link" href="/about/manufacturing-capabilities/#quality">View our quality-control approach ↗</a></div></div></section>

<section class="cms-section cms-order-section" id="ordering"><div class="container cms-order-layout"><div class="cms-order-intro"><span class="cms-eyebrow">From drawing to delivery</span><h2>A clear scope.<br /> A practical next step.</h2><p>Send the component drawing, quantity and destination. We review the route and acceptance requirements with you before production.</p><figure><img src="/images/manufacturing-split/real-assets/welding-workshop.jpg" alt="Robotic welding stations pictured in the REALJET company profile" width="1047" height="580" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Robotic welding</figcaption></figure></div><div class="cms-order-steps"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Share your requirement</h3><p>Drawing and revision, material, finish, quantity and destination. Arrange confidentiality before exchanging controlled files.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Confirm the route</h3><p>Resolve datums, welds, tooling, process order, external operations and the inspection records in the quotation.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Review the first article</h3><p>Agree a sample or pilot quantity and required results. Record approved changes before repeat production.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>Release for delivery</h3><p>Confirm final checks, identification, packing protection and transport responsibilities.</p></div></article></div></div></section>

<section class="mh-section" id="faq"><div class="container mh-faq-layout"><div><span class="mh-kicker">Before you enquire</span><h2>OEM manufacturing questions</h2><p>Define what you want manufactured and how it will be accepted.</p></div><div class="mh-faqs">{% for faq in manufacturingSplit.faqs %}<details{% if loop.first %} open{% endif %}><summary>{{ faq.question }}</summary><p>{{ faq.answer }}</p></details>{% endfor %}</div></div></section>

